      timeline: [
        '1939: Created at the Jockey Club of Montevideo, Uruguay.',
        '1940s: Spreads to Argentina and South America.',
        '1950: Rules standardized in North America (Classic Canasta).',
        '1950s: Global crazeâ€”nearly displaces Contract Bridge in popularity.',
        'Present: Two main variantsâ€”Classic Canasta (worldwide) and Modern American Canasta (North America).',
      ],
      evolution: 'The 1950 North American codification standardized 11-card deal, discard pile take mechanics, and canasta bonuses. Modern American Canasta (post-1960s) introduced more complex rules around wild cards, red/black threes distinctions, and going-out requirements.',
      cultural: 'A 1950s social phenomenon. Canasta clubs formed internationally. Associated with post-war prosperity and suburban social life in America and Europe.',
